<title>USA: Sensormatic Q3 shr $0.08 vs loss $0.68.</title>
<headline>Sensormatic Q3 shr $0.08 vs loss $0.68.</headline>
<dateline>BOCA RATON, Fla. 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sensormatic Electronics Corp</p>
<p>		     Consolidated Statements of Operations</p>
<p>			  For the Periods Ended March 31,</p>
<p>			  ($ Millions, Except Per Share)</p>
<p>					Third Quarter     Year-to-Date</p>
<p>			     F/Y 1997  F/Y 1996  F/Y 1997  F/Y 1996</p>
<p>						    (a)		   (a)</p>
<p>    Total revenues		250.1   225.3     752.7   737.1</p>
<p>  Restructuring charges	     -    42.5	   -    85.3</p>
<p>Total op. costs and</p>
<p>     expenses		     235.1   298.4     709.5   880.3</p>
<p> Operating income (loss)	15.0  (73.1)	43.2  (143.2)</p>
<p> Net income (loss)		  5.8  (50.0)	14.0  (98.2)</p>
<p> Earnings (Loss) per share     0.08  (0.68)	0.19  (1.33)</p>
<p>Primary Shares Outstanding:</p>
<p>				     74,381  73,788    74,225  73,502</p>
<p>(a) Effective fiscal year 1997, the company has included its customer engineering expenses as a component of &quot;cost of sales.&quot;  Customer engineering costs were previously included in &quot;selling, customer support and administrative expenses.&quot; Prior year amounts have been reclassified to conform to the fiscal year 1997 presentation.</p>
<p>The company said the third quarter of 1996 includes a special charge of $0.66 per share. Excluding the effect of restructuring and special charges, the net loss in that quarter is $1.4 million, or $0.02 per share.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
